    <string name="privacy_text">QR has no ads or analytics. The camera reads codes on the phone, without internet, and keeps no pictures. The history lives only on this phone, out of cloud backups. Links never open by themselves: you check them and open them with a tap. Only if you turn on MCP mode, the AI you connect with a token can read your history (without Wi‑Fi passwords) and make codes; with a read-and-write token also keep or delete them, through the relay. Exporting and importing the history use only the file you pick, and text you share with QR only fills in «Create». «Share a contact» reads only the contact you pick, on the phone: it is not uploaded, not kept in the history and the AI never sees it.</string>
